  "answer": "The goal was not met. Only one setting was confirmed as challenging: scene 19f339ba with the lead car 2 s earlier at 0.5x speed (S17). Even there, the policy never rear-ended the lead car. In each failed run the lead was more than about 50 m ahead or out of sight, the policy braked hard for no visible reason, and replayed traffic coming from behind, which does not react to the ego, ran into it. Its front-corner overlap counted as a front collision. So S17 shows a confirmed failure caused by phantom braking, but the collision itself depends on traffic being replayed rather than reacting. No setting on any scene showed VaVAM driving into a lead car that slows or stops. The other seven scenes had no failures, though most settings there ran only once or twice, so their ranges still allow substantial failure rates.",
